<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Grimnitz</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1529">1529</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of Grimnitz was concluded on 26 August 1529 at the Grimnitz hunting lodge between Elector Joachim I of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a> and the dukes of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pomerania">Pomerania</a>. Brandenburg gave up its claim to feudal overlordship over Pomerania, and in return the Griffin dukes recognised the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-hohenzollern">Hohenzollerns</a>' right to inherit the duchy if their own line died out. Brandenburg pressed this claim after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-griffins">Griffins</a> became extinct in 1637.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-grimnitz.jpg" alt="Treaty of Grimnitz" width="320" height="425" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Lucas Cranach the Elder · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lucas_Cranach_(I)_-_Joachim_I_Nestor_-_Jagdschloss_Grunewald.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
